---
layout: base.njk
title: "NaturalCloud™"
summary: "NaturalCloud™ securely stores authentication records and NaturalDetect™ test results, giving companies a centralized view of verification activity."
permalink: /naturalcloud/
---

{# The product mark, blended into the hero rather than sitting in a panel.
   Kirsty asked for the product icons to be somewhere on the page once the
   hero panel became a photograph. Same technique as the call-to-action
   watermark: the icon is a mask, so the colour comes from the stylesheet
   and the mark sits tonally on this page's own tint instead of being
   stamped on it in whatever colour the file happens to be.

   The class only appears when a mark is set, so clearing the field in the
   panel removes it. The url filter is required: HtmlBasePlugin does not
   look inside a style attribute. #}
<section class="challenge hero-cloud{% if naturalcloud.hero.mark %} solution-hero-mark{% endif %}"
  style="padding-top:9rem{% if naturalcloud.hero.mark %};--hero-mark:url('{{ naturalcloud.hero.mark | url }}'){% endif %}">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="challenge-grid">
      <div class="challenge-text">
        <span class="section-label">{{ naturalcloud.hero.label }}</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">{{ naturalcloud.hero.title }}</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">{{ naturalcloud.hero.tagline }}</p>
        <p class="challenge-lead" style="margin-top:1.5rem">{{ naturalcloud.hero.intro }}</p>
        <p class="challenge-sub">{{ naturalcloud.features.title }}</p>
        <ul class="challenge-list">
          {% for item in naturalcloud.features.items %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:2rem">
          <a href="{{ naturalcloud.final_cta.primary_url }}" class="btn btn-primary" style="cursor:pointer">{{ naturalcloud.final_cta.primary }}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      {# The video if there is one, then a photograph, then the logo panel.
         All three come from the data file, so which one shows is a CMS choice
         and not a code change.

         muted is not decoration: no browser will autoplay a video with sound,
         so without it the thing simply does not start. playsinline stops iOS
         taking it fullscreen the moment it plays. There is no audio track at
         all, so nothing is being silenced.

         preload="metadata" and not "none". Those two were tried the other way
         round and the video simply never started: autoplay and preload="none"
         contradict each other, since a browser cannot play what it has been
         told not to fetch. Measured at 0x0 natural size and paused after
         nearly three seconds on a local 216KB file.

         The 25KB poster is what keeps the panel from being empty in the
         meantime, and it is the video's own first frame, so the switch from
         still to moving is invisible. #}
      {% if naturalcloud.hero.video %}
      <div class="solution-photo solution-video">
        <video
          src="{{ naturalcloud.hero.video }}"
          {% if naturalcloud.hero.video_poster %}poster="{{ naturalcloud.hero.video_poster }}"{% endif %}
          autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"
          aria-label="{{ naturalcloud.hero.video_alt }}"></video>
      </div>
      {% elif naturalcloud.hero.image %}
      <div class="solution-photo">
        <img src="{{ naturalcloud.hero.image }}" alt="{{ naturalcloud.hero.image_alt }}" loading="lazy"
          style="{% if naturalcloud.hero.image_position %}object-position:{{ naturalcloud.hero.image_position }};{% endif %}{% if naturalcloud.hero.image_zoom %}--photo-zoom:{{ naturalcloud.hero.image_zoom }};--photo-zoom-origin:{{ naturalcloud.hero.image_position or "center" }}{% endif %}">
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="solution-mark">
        <img src="{{ naturalcloud.hero.logo }}" alt="{{ naturalcloud.hero.logo_alt }}" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="finalcta">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="finalcta-inner">
      <h2>{{ naturalcloud.final_cta.secondary }}</h2>
      <div class="finalcta-actions">
        <a href="{{ naturalcloud.final_cta.primary_url }}" class="btn btn-white" style="cursor:pointer">{{ naturalcloud.final_cta.primary }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
